{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Wealth</b>, <b>many</b>, <b>all</b> — four joined [terms]. And in the fifth he indicated the praise of one who grants to the poor and the disgrace of one who squanders his wealth on friends." "<b>Will add friends</b> — to his friends; and when he is poor, he separates from his friend, for his friend distances him until he separates from him. And it is possible that it means: a false witness — therefore he became impoverished."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:36.543670147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}